{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcosahedralCharacterGoldenRatio","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcosahedralCharacterGoldenRatio","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.icosahedral_ell1_fivefold_char_eq_golden","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.icosahedral_ell1_fivefold_char_eq_golden","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/IcosahedralCharacterGoldenRatio.lean#L30-L39","doc":"**The ℓ=1 icosahedral character on the 5-fold rotation is the golden ratio.**\n\n`χ_{ℓ=1}(2π/5) = 1 + 2cos(2π/5) = (1 + √5)/2`.  The exact, parameter-free\nfingerprint validating the `irrepToRotation` angle assignment (T₁ ← ℓ=1). ","signatureChunk":0}]}